  "title": "Federal Government Weekly Delta — September 21–25, 2026",
  "question": "What materially changed across official U.S. federal sources during September 21–25 after reconciliation to the September 22 deep-review baseline?",
  "bluf": "After the September 22 baseline, the strongest new federal movement was procedural rather than a single government-wide program: DOT finalized individualized DBE/ACDBE eligibility, OFAC consolidated sanctions-penalty procedure, the FTC changed practice and ethics-clearance rules, USPS updated NEPA procedure and the Supreme Court kept Missouri's 2022 congressional map controlling for the underway election. EXIM's up-to-$7-billion Argentina framework, CMS's 37-state voluntary quality pledge, VA's planned partial Compact-health implementation and ATF's future-effective explosives rule are real but do not yet prove commitments, payments, operation or outcomes. Current Fed, SEC, Treasury, UNGA, defense and country work remains with existing owners.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-25T23:59:59-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The human weekly window is September 21–25. New discovery is strictly after the September 22 deep-review cutoff at 11:51:46 EDT, with boundary replay for date-only and delayed-publication sources.",
  "use_note": "Use for the post-September-22 weekly material-change answer through Friday close. Follow folded topics to their current owners. Keep proposals, frameworks, voluntary pledges, rules, court orders, oversight findings, obligations, payments, deliveries and effects separate. Registration does not authorize Chronicle promotion, a canonical watch, Federal Group mutation, app/site shipment, commit or push.",
